SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Fails to Adopt Draft Resolution on Ending Ukraine Crisis, as Russian Federation Wields Veto","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14808.doc.htm","claim":"India abstained on the draft resolution and said there was no alternative to negotiation, while also citing concern for the welfare and security of Indians in Ukraine.","locator":"India delegation remarks after the vote","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN meeting record with a named delegation and recorded vote explanation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This is the Indian government position under Modi, not a private statement by him.","contrary_evidence":["An abstention is weaker than an affirmative condemnation vote and can reflect hedging as well as restraint."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Calls Emergency Special Session of General Assembly on Ukraine Crisis, Adopting Resolution 2623 (2022) by 11 Votes in Favour, 1 Against, 3 Abstentions","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14809.doc.htm","claim":"India abstained on the procedural resolution and its representative again called for an immediate cessation of hostilities and a return to diplomacy.","locator":"India delegation remarks after the vote","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN record and vote summary from the same day.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government position under Modi; not a private order or battlefield act.","contrary_evidence":["The vote avoided taking a sharper public position against Russia, so it is not unambiguous moral leadership."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Overwhelmingly Adopts Resolution Demanding Russian Federation Immediately End Illegal Use of Force in Ukraine, Withdraw All Troops","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12407.doc.htm","claim":"India abstained on the resolution demanding Russia end the use of force and withdraw, with the delegation saying it was considering the totality of circumstances and the situation of Indian nationals.","locator":"India delegation explanation in the statements-after-adoption section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official General Assembly vote record and delegation statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State position under Modi’s premiership, not a personal command decision.","contrary_evidence":["Abstention here again shows caution and nonalignment rather than full support for the resolution's coercive language."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Phone call between Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi and H.E. Emmanuel Macron, President of the French Republic","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-03-01","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1802188","claim":"Modi reiterated India's appeal for cessation of hostilities and a return to dialogue and diplomacy, and briefed Macron on evacuations and urgent relief supplies including medicines.","locator":"paragraphs on Ukraine and humanitarian assistance","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release, dated and attributable to the Prime Minister.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler speech in office.","contrary_evidence":["This is a bilateral diplomatic readout, so it is useful evidence of posture but not proof that India changed the conflict's trajectory."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM speaks with His Excellency President Volodymyr Zelenskyy of Ukraine","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-03-07","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1803516","claim":"Modi told Zelenskyy that India stood for peaceful resolution and direct dialogue, while expressing deep concern over the humanitarian crisis and the safety of Indians still in Ukraine.","locator":"opening paragraph of the release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release from the PMO/PIB on the day of the call.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement as Prime Minister.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is diplomatic rhetoric unless paired with concrete policy follow-through, which is only partially visible here."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"प्रधानमंत्री श्री नरेन्द्र मोदी ने यूक्रेन से भारतीयों को सुरक्षित निकालने के लिए शुरू किए गए ऑपरेशन गंगा में शामिल हितधारकों से वर्चुअल तौर पर मुलाकात की","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-03-15","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1806387","claim":"Operation Ganga successfully evacuated about 23,000 Indian citizens and 147 foreign nationals from Ukraine.","locator":"lead paragraph of the Hindi release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release in Hindi, directly dated and attributable to the Prime Minister's Office.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct government action under Modi's leadership; it reflects humanitarian crisis management rather than combat command.","contrary_evidence":["Evacuation success shows protection of nationals, but it does not by itself answer broader questions about India’s stance on the war."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"English Translation of Remarks by Prime Minister, Shri Narendra Modi at virtual meeting with the President of the USA","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1849770","claim":"Modi said he had appealed to both Putin and Zelenskyy for peace, condemned the Bucha killings, said India had sent medicines and relief materials to Ukraine and neighbouring countries, and urged direct talks.","locator":"paragraphs beginning 'The news of the recent killings...' and 'We have sent medicines and other relief materials...'","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government transcription/translation of the PM’s remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement, though still self-reported diplomacy.","contrary_evidence":["The source is an official translation and a self-presentation of policy, so it should be triangulated with UN records and other diplomatic readouts."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.6","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Text to Suspend Russian Federation from Human Rights Council, Continuing Emergency Special Session on Humanitarian Crisis in Ukraine","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-04-07","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12414.doc.htm","claim":"India abstained on the Human Rights Council suspension text and said it had stood for peace, dialogue and diplomacy since the start of the Ukraine conflict, while also condemning Bucha killings and calling for an independent investigation.","locator":"India delegation remarks in the statements-after-adoption section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN vote record and delegation explanation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government position under Modi’s premiership.","contrary_evidence":["Abstaining on a human-rights accountability vote despite atrocity allegations cuts against a strongly punitive or confrontational line."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.6","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Visit of the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom to India (April 21-22, 2022)","publisher":"Prime Minister of India","publication_date":"2022-04-21","url":"https://www.pmindia.gov.in/en/news_updates/visit-of-the-prime-minister-of-the-united-kingdom-to-india-april-21-22-2022/","claim":"Modi expressed deep concern at the mounting humanitarian crisis in Ukraine and reiterated his call for an immediate cessation of violence and a return to direct dialogue and diplomacy.","locator":"paragraph 7 in the joint-statement summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO record of a dated bilateral statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler diplomacy in office.","contrary_evidence":["This is a diplomatic statement with no direct enforcement mechanism, so it shows posture more than measurable outcome."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Telephone Conversation between Prime Minister and President of Ukraine","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-10-04","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1865159&lang=2&reg=48","claim":"Modi called for an early cessation of hostilities, said there can be no military solution, and emphasized the importance of respecting the UN Charter and the safety of nuclear installations in Ukraine.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO/PIB release with a dated direct conversation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement and diplomatic action.","contrary_evidence":["The nuclear-installation point is relevant to catastrophic-risk avoidance, but the call still did not produce a settlement or verified de-escalation on the ground."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"17TH ROUND OF INDIA-CHINA CORPS COMMANDER LEVEL MEETING","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-12-22","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1885707","claim":"India and China said they had an open and constructive discussion, agreed to maintain security and stability on the ground, and would stay in close contact through military and diplomatic channels.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release on the bilateral border process.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level border management under Modi’s administration, not a personal command memo.","contrary_evidence":["The border dispute remained unresolved, so this is management of inherited tension rather than proof of settlement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Release of the 15th Round of China-India Corps Commander Level Meeting","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India","publication_date":"2022-03-12","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1805371","claim":"The two sides said dialogue through military and diplomatic channels should continue until a mutually acceptable resolution is reached, and that this would help restore peace and tranquility along the LAC.","locator":"body text of the joint release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government release on the border talks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional border-policy posture under Modi’s government.","contrary_evidence":["The release confirms continuing friction, so it is evidence of de-escalation management rather than a final peaceful settlement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Resolution Condemning Russian Federation’s Annexation of Four Eastern Ukraine Regions","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12458.doc.htm","claim":"India abstained on the resolution condemning Russia's annexation moves and urged an immediate cessation of hostilities, warning that an escalation of rhetoric and tension is in no one's interest.","locator":"India delegation remarks after adoption","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official General Assembly vote record and delegation statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government position under Modi.","contrary_evidence":["Again, abstention is more cautious than strongly punitive, so the vote shows hedging as well as peace advocacy."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across UN vote records, PMO/PIB bilateral statements, India-China border releases, evacuation notices, and a smaller set of Reuters-syndicated or later retrospective pages.

Retained because they were directly dated to 2022 and tied to actual ruler conduct:
- UN Security Council and General Assembly Ukraine votes and India’s explanations.
- Modi’s direct calls with Macron, Zelenskyy, and bilateral statements with the UK and the US.
- Operation Ganga evacuation material, including the Hindi PIB release.
- India-China border talks in March and December 2022.

Rejected or not used:
- Later retrospectives from 2023-2025 that described the same Ukraine or border posture but were out of period for this chapter.
- Generic diplomatic pages that repeated “peace” language without a dated decision, call, vote, or operational action.
- Older inherited-context India-China documents from before 2022 that were useful background but not target-period evidence.
- Duplicate evacuation notices and duplicate PMO summaries that restated the same Operation Ganga facts without adding a materially distinct claim.
- Economic or trade reporting on Russia-India ties that was relevant to context but not directly to international peace conduct.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Public evidence is still thin on internal decision-making: we can see the votes, calls, and releases, but not the cabinet-level reasoning behind each abstention or statement.
- There is limited direct public evidence on how much Modi personally controlled the India-China border posture beyond the official releases.
- I did not find a strong 2022 source showing a consequential ceasefire negotiation that Modi personally advanced to completion, so the record is one of restraint and diplomacy rather than settlement success.
- If you want, I can do a second pass focused only on India’s 2022 UN voting rationale and any local-language reporting on the border and Ukraine diplomacy.
